        "attribution": "Shor and Steane introduced landmark codes and fault-tolerance ideas, while Kitaev established a distinct topological route of foundational importance.",
        "maturity": "The principles have been extensively tested and now guide experimental hardware, although fully fault-tolerant computation remains unfinished.",
